Description: This project uses PyGame to simulate an 
n-body simulation, utilizing vectorized calculations of 
forces. There are two methods of integration currently 
implemented: Verlet integration and Euler integration. 
This program also includes toggleable collision detection, 
as well as energy tracking. 


Known Limitations: The simulation exhibits energy 
instability over time, particularly when collisions are disabled. 
This is primarily due to numerical integration error and 
sensitivity to timestep size. The program also becomes unstable 
when ~200 or more bodies are simulated at once. 
